Performance: real-time pacing, WAD in RAM, direct framebuffer, -fps.
 - I_GetTime from the TSC (calibrated against Stall), monotonic at 35 Hz;
   the RTC version had whole-second resolution and jumped back each minute
 - D_DoomLoop runs the tics real time asks for (max 4 catch-up) and draws
   once, instead of sleeping 1/35 s + one tic (game speed depended on frame
   time); the screen melt is paced the same way
 - each WAD is read into memory once; lumps no longer go through the
   firmware file I/O mid-game (that was the stutter). Zone 20 -> 64 MB
 - frames are written straight into a 32-bit RGB/BGR framebuffer, one
   expanded line copied frameScale times; GOP Blt stays as fallback (-blt)
 - -fps: HUD line with fps, ms/frame, drawing path, and the mouse resolution
   and peak movement the firmware reports (for -mousescale)
 - drop the mis-armed timer event and the per-call mallocs in I_GetTime

